{"id":"prop-agent","ord":"a0","title":"agent","desc":"Which agent a lane is dispatched to. A ROSTER, not a sum: the valid values are whatever nodes sit under `agents-root` right now, so adding an implementor is adding a node there and no declaration changes.\n\nThe value is the roster node's **id** (`agent-grok`), never its title — names rename, ids don't.","custom":{"type":"ref","under":"agents-root"}}
{"id":"prop-reviewer","ord":"a1","title":"reviewer","desc":"Who reviewed the lane's PR, from the same roster `agent` reads. Two keys and one place: an author and a reviewer are the same kind of thing, and a second roster would be a second answer about one list of people.","custom":{"type":"ref","under":"agents-root"}}
{"id":"prop-repo","ord":"a2","title":"repo","desc":"Which repository the work is in.\n\nThe variants are this node's own CHILDREN rather than a roster elsewhere, and that is a deviation from the plan's example worth naming: `docs/brainstorming/typed-properties.md` writes `{kind:\"ref\", under:\"repos-roster\"}`, and this vault has no repos roster to point at. Minting one inside a board file to match an example would be inventing structure the board does not have. Adding a repo is still adding a child row — the same gesture, one file over.","custom":{"type":"ref"}}
{"id":"repo-olai","parent":"prop-repo","ord":"a0","title":"olai","desc":"This repository — the project folder, and so the repo a bare `pr` means."}
{"id":"repo-kolu","parent":"prop-repo","ord":"a1","title":"kolu","desc":"juspay/kolu — the terminal fleet and the surface framework olai is built on."}
{"id":"repo-drishti","parent":"prop-repo","ord":"a2","title":"drishti","desc":"juspay/drishti."}
{"id":"prop-merge","ord":"a3","title":"merge","desc":"How the PR is to be merged — the word a driver switches on, and nothing else. The gate that was actually applied (which reviews folded, which measurement was accepted, whose word it was) is the interesting half and belongs in the note.","custom":{"type":"ref"}}
{"id":"merge-auto","parent":"prop-merge","ord":"a0","title":"auto","desc":"Merged by the pipeline on its stated gate — reviews folded and CI green — without a further word from the human."}
{"id":"merge-human","parent":"prop-merge","ord":"a1","title":"human","desc":"The human merges it, or says so explicitly. The standing merge gate (agents.olai's `merge-gate`) makes this the default; `auto` is the exception a class-wide ruling grants."}
{"id":"prop-dispatched","ord":"a4","title":"dispatched","desc":"When the lane was dispatched. A date and nothing else: the queue it came out of, and the mandate that filled that queue, are the note's.","custom":{"type":"date"}}
{"id":"prop-approved","ord":"a5","title":"approved","desc":"When the human approved the merge. The words of the approval go in the note — this key answers *when*, so a span can ask what was approved this week.","custom":{"type":"date"}}
{"id":"prop-retired","ord":"a6","title":"retired","desc":"When the item was retired. The verification it was retired against is the note's.","custom":{"type":"date"}}
{"id":"prop-verified","ord":"a7","title":"verified","desc":"When the claim was verified against the tree. What was checked, and against which commit, is the note's.","custom":{"type":"date"}}
{"id":"prop-merged","ord":"a8","title":"merged","desc":"When the PR merged — the EVENT. The artifact is `merge-commit` beside it, and the split is deliberate: this key held a sha for months while its name said otherwise, which is exactly the drift typing catches.","custom":{"type":"date"}}
{"id":"prop-pr-url","ord":"a9","title":"pr-url","desc":"The pull request, as its URL.\n\n**ONE key for every repo, and the value is the whole address** (ruled by the human 2026-08-25, amending Converged §2). The number-and-scope-rule shape this replaced — `pr` as an `int`, with `kolu-pr` and `drishti-pr` beside it and a rule about when a bare `pr` was legal — bought spans and cost a vocabulary: four keys for one fact, a rule a writer had to hold in their head about which one applied, and a door that still had to derive the URL from a repo ref plus a number before anything could be clicked.\n\nA URL carries the repo IN the value, so there is nothing to scope and nothing to derive: an agent parses the number or the repo out of it when it needs them, and the chip is already a door because a URL has always been one. Declared `text` — which is the honest kind for it, and the declaration is the blessing: this is a deliberate shape, not a value nobody cleaned up.\n\nA node tracking PRs in more than one repo holds a LIST, which is what `custom` has always meant by one — a fact can be several.","custom":{"type":"text"}}
{"id":"prop-merge-commit","ord":"aA","title":"merge-commit","desc":"The merge commit, as its URL — the ARTIFACT, where `merged` is the event.\n\nA URL for `pr-url`'s reason and by the same ruling (the human, 2026-08-25, amending Converged §3): the address carries the repo, so one key serves every repo and nothing has to be derived to make it clickable. It replaces the bare sha, and the `kolu-merge-commit` / `drishti-merge-commit` pair that a per-repo split had made necessary.\n\nDeclared `text`. A node with commits in more than one repo holds a list.","custom":{"type":"text"}}
{"id":"prop-brief","ord":"aB","title":"brief","desc":"The lane's brief.\n\n**Declared `path` and not `doc`, which is a compromise the human should rule on.** `doc` is what the plan asks for and is the stronger promise — a path that resolves to a document this directory actually serves. But `docs/briefs/` is GITIGNORED (`.gitignore:36`), exactly as `orchestrator/lanes.olai` is: the briefs exist in the orchestrator's working vault and are not part of the repository. Declared `doc`, every one of these values is a finding in any checkout that has not run a lane — including CI. Declared `path`, the shape is fenced and the promise that it names a served document is not made.\n\nThe honest fix is upstream of this file: either the briefs become tracked, or `doc` is right and a checkout without them is expected to be red. Not a decision to make silently inside a migration.","custom":{"type":"path"}}
{"id":"prop-worktree","ord":"aC","title":"worktree","desc":"The lane's worktree. A path, and it may point anywhere — it names a directory on the machine the orchestrator runs on, not something this vault serves.","custom":{"type":"path"}}
{"id":"prop-superseded-by","ord":"aD","title":"superseded-by","desc":"The node that replaced this one. A `node` rather than prose because the reference is the queryable half — `prop:superseded-by=x` answers \"what did this replace\" from either end. Pair it with a `superseded` date where when it happened matters.","custom":{"type":"node"}}
{"id":"prop-from","ord":"aE","title":"from","desc":"Where the item came from — a PR's deferral, a review, a debate, the human over lunch.\n\n**DECLARED text, and the declaration is the point.** Provenance is a sentence by nature, and this is the durable blessing in the one place a future tidier will look: the prose here is deliberate, not a value somebody failed to clean up. Not split into who/when — a design that could not hold `from` would be a record system, which this is not.","custom":{"type":"text"}}
{"id":"repo-xyne-boxes","parent":"prop-repo","ord":"a3","title":"xyne-boxes","desc":"juspay/xyne-boxes."}
{"id":"repo-odu","parent":"prop-repo","ord":"a4","title":"odu","desc":"juspay/odu — the CI harness's own repository."}
